From f709a9bfb87f4c6d789ee91f9e0a5e8ea53f9797 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:21:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] datamap: give every contacted address a server place
 (ADR-161)

The collector hands the first address of a lookup or connect to the service, which looks it up in the mapped ipmap.bin on the service thread, only for a service that has no place to draw yet, and keeps the kind, the country, the city with its coordinates, the AS number and the operator of the server, never the address. The place says where the server lies in the data, not where the company is based.

The history keeps it only when the user chose so: rows of seventeen fields that stay within the line limit of the decoder, a file written under a bound with the oldest days left out first, the choice in a file of its own that goes off with the history, and IDataMapService.setServerHistory at the end of the transaction order.

The Binder entry gains seven fields and the snapshot one. The entries of a reply are bounded in bytes as well as in number, and the evidence of a link is cut.
